  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Credit and Financial Services: Project to Improve Indigenous and Family Farming in Value Chains in the Eastern Region-PPI Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To contribute to increasing incomes and the quality of life of small family farmers and the poor rural population by means of their inclusion in value chains, on a sustainable basis and with a focus on gender and environmental concerns, through representative social organizations. With the additional financing, the project will be scaled up to include an additional 13,200 beneficiary families, equivalent to a population of about 66,000 persons, involved directly in some 70 Articulated Business Plans (known by their Spanish acronym PNAs) and 115 Microcapitalization Plans (PMC)</narrative>
  </description>
